WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.535 --> 00:00:04.537
- So I was thinking about
what to talk about tonight.

00:00:04.537 --> 00:00:07.240 align:start size:88% position:13%
I usually cover current
events on my show

00:00:07.240 --> 00:00:08.942
and I wanna briefly touch

00:00:08.942 --> 00:00:10.677
on what's going on
in Virginia first,

00:00:10.677 --> 00:00:12.545 align:start size:84% position:16%
which Rod just
referenced quickly.

00:00:13.380 --> 00:00:15.281
Because I think today,

00:00:15.281 --> 00:00:18.451 align:start size:94% position:6%
although I don't think
that most of the solutions

00:00:18.451 --> 00:00:19.719
that we are gonna need

00:00:19.719 --> 00:00:21.154
and hopefully we'll
find in this country

00:00:21.154 --> 00:00:23.590
will be purely through politics

00:00:23.590 --> 00:00:25.358
and certainly through
the political class

00:00:25.358 --> 00:00:26.726
that we have right now.

00:00:26.726 --> 00:00:29.462
I do think today
is an incredibly,

00:00:29.462 --> 00:00:34.467 align:start position:0%
incredibly important moment
for the future of this country.

00:00:35.668 --> 00:00:36.803
What's happening in
Virginia right now

00:00:36.803 --> 00:00:39.172 align:start size:88% position:13%
is sort of a bellwether
for everything

00:00:39.172 --> 00:00:40.807 align:start size:84% position:16%
that this conference
has been about.

00:00:40.807 --> 00:00:44.310 align:start size:84% position:16%
If wokeism and leftism
and collectivism

00:00:44.310 --> 00:00:46.613
is gonna continue
to be on the march,

00:00:47.580 --> 00:00:48.915
it's gonna go through McAuliffe,

00:00:48.915 --> 00:00:50.150
it's gonna go through Virginia.

00:00:50.150 --> 00:00:52.118 align:start size:84% position:16%
And suddenly in
the last two weeks,

00:00:52.118 --> 00:00:54.988 align:start size:88% position:13%
it feels like maybe
that isn't gonna happen.

00:00:54.988 --> 00:00:57.991
And I try not to
spend too much time

00:00:57.991 --> 00:01:01.394
on the self-imposed mental
institution that is Twitter,

00:01:01.394 --> 00:01:04.197 align:start size:88% position:13%
but I was looking around
Twitter this morning

00:01:04.197 --> 00:01:06.199
and you can sort of feel it.

00:01:06.199 --> 00:01:08.201 align:start size:81% position:19%
You can sort of
feel people going,

00:01:08.201 --> 00:01:10.437
man, the anti-woke people,

00:01:10.437 --> 00:01:13.706
if we can get a win and it
doesn't even necessarily mean

00:01:13.706 --> 00:01:15.575 align:start size:88% position:13%
that we love everything
about Youngkin.

00:01:15.575 --> 00:01:17.377 align:start size:97% position:3%
It doesn't mean that we
agree with all his policies

00:01:17.377 --> 00:01:19.612 align:start position:0%
or think he's the best
politician or any of that stuff

00:01:19.612 --> 00:01:22.549
or that politicians are the
ones to fix it, as I said.

00:01:22.549 --> 00:01:25.452 align:start size:94% position:6%
But if we can get a win
right now, just something,

00:01:25.452 --> 00:01:27.821 align:start size:84% position:16%
that it might start
the turnaround.

00:01:27.821 --> 00:01:29.289
I think we can all feel that,

00:01:29.289 --> 00:01:32.659 align:start size:97% position:3%
we're finally all kind of
having enough of this, right?

00:01:32.659 --> 00:01:33.593
We let it happen.

00:01:33.593 --> 00:01:35.361
I referenced this last night,

00:01:35.361 --> 00:01:38.264
it was like all of these
kids that were in college

00:01:38.264 --> 00:01:41.534
with blue hair and genderless
and screaming at professors

00:01:41.534 --> 00:01:43.837
and causing what was it,

00:01:43.837 --> 00:01:47.507 align:start size:88% position:13%
Berkeley to spend
something like $400,000

00:01:47.507 --> 00:01:50.443 align:start size:84% position:16%
to secure the campus
when very scary

00:01:50.443 --> 00:01:53.113
4'7" Ben Shapiro showed up.

00:01:53.113 --> 00:01:55.582
It's like, he's very small.

00:01:55.582 --> 00:01:57.984 align:start size:97% position:3%
He's actually in my pocket.
You guys wanna see him?

00:02:01.988 --> 00:02:05.258
There's a feeling though that
they've overstepped, right?

00:02:05.258 --> 00:02:08.595 align:start size:94% position:6%
They've really overstepped
by coming for the kids.

00:02:08.595 --> 00:02:12.999
First, we're gonna inject
the kids with the vaccine,

00:02:12.999 --> 00:02:14.934 align:start size:94% position:6%
and it really doesn't
even matter what you think

00:02:14.934 --> 00:02:17.904
about vaccines and
in a certain respect,

00:02:17.904 --> 00:02:20.006
it doesn't even matter what
you think about mandates.

00:02:20.006 --> 00:02:23.776 align:start position:0%
The fact that the FDA, I'm
sure many of you saw the video,

00:02:23.776 --> 00:02:27.113 align:start size:88% position:13%
just a few days ago, the
FDA board was talking

00:02:27.113 --> 00:02:29.516 align:start size:84% position:16%
about vaccine
mandates for children.

00:02:29.516 --> 00:02:33.586
And one of the doctors
actually said on video,

00:02:33.586 --> 00:02:35.088
"We don't know what it'll do,

00:02:35.088 --> 00:02:37.290
that's why we have to
give it to the kids."

00:02:37.290 --> 00:02:40.627
I mean, this is the
level of craziness

00:02:40.627 --> 00:02:43.096
that we are dealing with, right?

00:02:43.096 --> 00:02:46.733 align:start size:88% position:13%
They are using our
children as experiments.

00:02:46.733 --> 00:02:49.936 align:start position:0%
They are putting people in masks
and locking people at home.

00:02:49.936 --> 00:02:53.573 align:start position:0%
We know all of the endless
things that this is doing to us

00:02:53.573 --> 00:02:56.142
psychologically and culturally.

00:02:56.142 --> 00:02:59.612
I come from a place
called California.

00:03:00.713 --> 00:03:02.749
Thank you. One person booing it.

00:03:02.749 --> 00:03:05.318 align:start size:94% position:6%
The one other Californian
here, obviously,

00:03:06.719 --> 00:03:09.322
where it's like living
in another country truly.

00:03:09.322 --> 00:03:11.357 align:start size:84% position:16%
I mean, these last
couple days in Florida

00:03:11.357 --> 00:03:12.725
where I've seen your faces,

00:03:12.725 --> 00:03:16.062 align:start size:84% position:16%
people smile and
aren't afraid of you.

00:03:16.062 --> 00:03:20.200 align:start size:97% position:3%
I mean, we've done something
so incredibly dangerous

00:03:20.200 --> 00:03:22.802 align:start size:84% position:16%
and look how
quickly they did it.

00:03:22.802 --> 00:03:24.003
Look how quickly they did it.

00:03:24.003 --> 00:03:25.271 align:start size:81% position:19%
And that's why
last night I said,

00:03:25.271 --> 00:03:26.806
you have to give the
devil his due here.

00:03:26.806 --> 00:03:28.975
We can all run around and
say wokeism is ridiculous

00:03:28.975 --> 00:03:30.210
and these people are buffoons

00:03:30.210 --> 00:03:31.744 align:start size:88% position:13% line:0%
and they don't know what
they're talking about

00:03:31.744 --> 00:03:34.881 line:0%
and okay, fine, so be it,
they all seem like clowns,

00:03:34.881 --> 00:03:37.083 line:0%
but you kinda have
to admire it, right?

00:03:37.083 --> 00:03:41.221 align:start size:94% position:6%
Look how much destruction
they have created

00:03:41.221 --> 00:03:42.655
in really a couple years.

00:03:42.655 --> 00:03:44.424 align:start size:97% position:3%
And I know we can talk
about sort of the long march

00:03:44.424 --> 00:03:45.959
through the institutions

00:03:45.959 --> 00:03:48.661
and this was all happening
in colleges 20 years ago.

00:03:48.661 --> 00:03:50.096
I get it.

00:03:50.096 --> 00:03:53.233 align:start size:94% position:6%
I talk to some of my
conservative friends now,

00:03:53.233 --> 00:03:56.336
people that I thought were
very scary right-wingers

00:03:56.336 --> 00:03:59.272 align:start size:97% position:3%
like Dennis Prager and
Larry Elder and Glenn Beck.

00:03:59.272 --> 00:04:00.773 align:start size:84% position:16%
And I'll say something
and they'll go,

00:04:00.773 --> 00:04:02.709
"Yeah, Dave, that's what
I was saying 30 years ago.

00:04:02.709 --> 00:04:04.544
Thank you, appreciate that."

00:04:05.979 --> 00:04:09.349
But just in the last couple
years, fueled by big tech,

00:04:09.349 --> 00:04:12.118 align:start size:88% position:13%
this woke thing has
done so much disruption.

00:04:12.118 --> 00:04:13.620
And that's why I really do think

00:04:13.620 --> 00:04:16.689
that this election today in
Virginia is so important.

00:04:16.689 --> 00:04:18.891
And it's funny because
I live in California.

00:04:18.891 --> 00:04:20.360
Here we are in Florida.

00:04:20.360 --> 00:04:24.163
It should probably have nothing
to do with any of us, right?

00:04:24.163 --> 00:04:26.933 align:start size:84% position:16%
Unless any of you
here live in Virginia,

00:04:26.933 --> 00:04:28.835 align:start size:88% position:13%
in which case I hope
you voted a couple times

00:04:28.835 --> 00:04:29.836
before you got here.

00:04:32.005 --> 00:04:33.940
Unless you do, it
really shouldn't

00:04:33.940 --> 00:04:35.141
have anything to do with this.

00:04:35.141 --> 00:04:36.976 align:start size:84% position:16%
I mean, the Federalist
system was set up

00:04:36.976 --> 00:04:39.712 align:start position:0%
so that the states would be
separate and mostly independent

00:04:39.712 --> 00:04:41.247 align:start size:94% position:6%
and the federal government
would do a little bit

00:04:41.247 --> 00:04:43.283
to make sure we're
in essence not at war

00:04:43.283 --> 00:04:44.917 align:start size:84% position:16%
and we're having
trade with each other

00:04:44.917 --> 00:04:46.819
and things of that nature,

00:04:46.819 --> 00:04:48.821 align:start size:84% position:16%
but suddenly it
feels very important.

00:04:48.821 --> 00:04:50.923
It feels very important
that this Virginia race

00:04:50.923 --> 00:04:52.458
go the right way,

00:04:52.458 --> 00:04:54.027
because one of the things that
I talk about often on my show

00:04:54.027 --> 00:04:56.129
is we need a little hope.

00:04:56.129 --> 00:04:57.664
I toured with Jordan Peterson,

00:04:57.664 --> 00:04:59.832
he would often talk about
that star in the distance.

00:04:59.832 --> 00:05:01.367
He would reference "Pinocchio"

00:05:01.367 --> 00:05:02.835
and "When You Wish Upon A Star".

00:05:02.835 --> 00:05:05.438 align:start size:97% position:3%
And I think we've sort of lost
that in America right now,

00:05:05.438 --> 00:05:06.839
we're all sort of
wandering around.

00:05:06.839 --> 00:05:08.441
We wake up every morning,

00:05:08.441 --> 00:05:10.310
you go online or
you watch the news,

00:05:10.310 --> 00:05:12.679
you see the next
ridiculous thing

00:05:12.679 --> 00:05:14.881
that these people
are throwing on us,

00:05:14.881 --> 00:05:19.018 align:start size:97% position:3%
whether it's the gender stuff
or the vaccination stuff,

00:05:20.219 --> 00:05:21.988
or now Joe Biden is
gonna solve climate.

00:05:21.988 --> 00:05:24.223 align:start size:97% position:3%
I mean, the guy fell asleep
at the talk yesterday.

00:05:24.223 --> 00:05:25.391
Did you see that?

00:05:25.391 --> 00:05:28.461 align:start size:88% position:13%
Like, we are just
inundated with stupidity

00:05:28.461 --> 00:05:30.930
and we need some hope.

00:05:30.930 --> 00:05:34.534
So I think today
there is some hope

00:05:34.534 --> 00:05:37.136
and I'll be talking
with Jonathan Isaac,

00:05:37.136 --> 00:05:39.038
who you guys might know,

00:05:39.038 --> 00:05:41.674 align:start size:88% position:13%
who's the Orlando Magic
basketball player,

00:05:41.674 --> 00:05:43.309 align:start size:84% position:16%
who's come out against
vaccine mandates.

00:05:43.309 --> 00:05:46.245
We just had a little talk.
I'm gonna talk to him, yeah.

00:05:46.245 --> 00:05:48.981
(crowd clapping)

00:05:50.450 --> 00:05:52.485
It's not an easy feat
for a guy like him.

00:05:52.485 --> 00:05:54.220
Kyrie Irving is the one
that most people know,

00:05:54.220 --> 00:05:55.722
he's a big star.

00:05:55.722 --> 00:05:58.291
The guy's probably got 80
million bucks or something.

00:05:58.291 --> 00:06:00.360
Jonathan Isaac's only been
in league for a couple years.

00:06:00.360 --> 00:06:02.995
He has a huge, bright future
that he's put on the line,

00:06:02.995 --> 00:06:04.864
but I don't know if
it's even public yet,

00:06:04.864 --> 00:06:09.268
but I'll be interviewing
him tonight right up here

00:06:09.268 --> 00:06:10.670
before J. D. Vance speaks,

00:06:10.670 --> 00:06:13.206 align:start size:84% position:16%
and he's ready to step
into a wider world

00:06:13.206 --> 00:06:15.842 align:start size:97% position:3%
and realize that I don't know
that he considers himself

00:06:15.842 --> 00:06:18.311
a conservative or a Republican

00:06:18.311 --> 00:06:20.680
or that he'd ever
thought he'd talk

00:06:20.680 --> 00:06:21.881
at a conference like this,

00:06:21.881 --> 00:06:23.783 align:start size:84% position:16%
but he was very
excited to come here

00:06:23.783 --> 00:06:25.385
and we need that sort of thing.

00:06:25.385 --> 00:06:28.421 align:start size:84% position:16%
We need more and more
people to realize

00:06:28.421 --> 00:06:31.190
that the machine is
not gonna save us.

00:06:31.190 --> 00:06:34.026 align:start size:84% position:16%
And again, great,
let's get Youngkin in.

00:06:34.026 --> 00:06:36.929 align:start size:97% position:3%
Let's hopefully get a little
signal out to the system

00:06:36.929 --> 00:06:38.998
that things can turn around,

00:06:38.998 --> 00:06:42.301 align:start size:84% position:16%
but it's just not
the politicians that
are gonna save us.

00:06:42.301 --> 00:06:45.371
It's us that is gonna save
us. That really is the truth.

00:06:45.371 --> 00:06:48.107
(crowd clapping)

00:06:50.209 --> 00:06:51.978
So I was thinking,

00:06:51.978 --> 00:06:55.982 align:start size:97% position:3%
a lot of people know I
would say roughly my story.

00:06:55.982 --> 00:06:57.583
I was a lefty, I
was a progressive.

00:06:57.583 --> 00:07:00.887 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then there's a
moment that has been seen

00:07:00.887 --> 00:07:04.757
probably 50 million times or
something like that on YouTube.

00:07:04.757 --> 00:07:07.827
Where as a lefty, I sat
down with a conservative

00:07:07.827 --> 00:07:09.929 align:start size:94% position:6%
or really libertarian talk
show host, Larry Elder,

00:07:09.929 --> 00:07:11.464
who you all know.

00:07:11.464 --> 00:07:13.866
And we started talking about
systemic racism and I said,

00:07:13.866 --> 00:07:16.936 align:start size:84% position:16%
"Larry, but what about
systemic racism?"

00:07:16.936 --> 00:07:18.471
And as a lefty,

00:07:18.471 --> 00:07:20.239
I kind of just believed it
existed because I said it.

00:07:20.239 --> 00:07:22.708 align:start size:97% position:3%
And that's really what they
believe about a lot of things.

00:07:22.708 --> 00:07:23.976
You just say something

00:07:23.976 --> 00:07:25.645
and well, I said it,
so it must be true.

00:07:25.645 --> 00:07:27.747
And I'm sure most of
you have seen the clip,

00:07:27.747 --> 00:07:29.615 align:start size:84% position:16%
but Larry really
just disassembled me.

00:07:29.615 --> 00:07:34.086
He did it just beautifully
and sort of like operating.

00:07:34.086 --> 00:07:37.723
He just had stats and numbers
and went through everything.

00:07:37.723 --> 00:07:39.659 align:start size:97% position:3%
And I don't know how many
people can say that their best

00:07:39.659 --> 00:07:43.596 align:start size:97% position:3%
and worst career moment
were at the exact same time.

00:07:43.596 --> 00:07:45.965
But I really believe that
I can say that about myself

00:07:45.965 --> 00:07:49.101 align:start size:97% position:3%
because it was my worst moment
for very obvious reasons.

00:07:49.101 --> 00:07:52.238 align:start size:97% position:3%
I got into a debate not
ready, not armed with facts,

00:07:52.238 --> 00:07:54.707
not ready to counter
the ideas of someone

00:07:54.707 --> 00:07:55.708
who I really should have known

00:07:55.708 --> 00:07:57.109
has been doing this for 30 years

00:07:57.109 --> 00:07:59.212 align:start size:81% position:19%
and he wasn't just
gonna lay over

00:07:59.212 --> 00:08:02.648
and just let me run across him.

00:08:02.648 --> 00:08:04.150
But I think it was
my best moment also

00:08:04.150 --> 00:08:06.919
because at the time
we were on Ora TV,

00:08:06.919 --> 00:08:08.855
I had a big staff
in the control room

00:08:08.855 --> 00:08:11.791 align:start size:94% position:6%
and we taped it and it was
gonna air the next day.

00:08:11.791 --> 00:08:13.326
And I walked into
the control room

00:08:13.326 --> 00:08:16.863
and the producers said to
me, "Dave, we'll cut that.

00:08:16.863 --> 00:08:18.130
We'll cut that moment.

00:08:18.130 --> 00:08:19.866
We're obviously not
gonna put that up."

00:08:19.866 --> 00:08:22.668 align:start size:97% position:3%
And I don't know what was
going on in my head exactly,

00:08:22.668 --> 00:08:26.405
but I thought, no, we
have to leave that.

00:08:26.405 --> 00:08:29.342
That was the true moment.

00:08:29.342 --> 00:08:30.443
If yeah...

00:08:30.443 --> 00:08:33.212
(crowd clapping)

00:08:34.780 --> 00:08:37.316
If there's any purpose
of being an interviewer

00:08:37.316 --> 00:08:39.552
or trying to explain to
people what I believe

00:08:39.552 --> 00:08:41.988
or listening to people
who know more than me,

00:08:41.988 --> 00:08:43.456 align:start size:84% position:16%
then when something
true happens,

00:08:43.456 --> 00:08:45.191
we certainly can't cut that.

00:08:45.191 --> 00:08:47.693
And over the next couple days,

00:08:47.693 --> 00:08:52.064 align:start size:97% position:3%
it got cut across YouTube
and all the usual headlines,

00:08:52.064 --> 00:08:54.834 align:start size:97% position:3%
conservative destroys
libtard and the rest of it.

00:08:54.834 --> 00:08:57.870
And I was like, oh God, what
a headache this is gonna be.

00:08:57.870 --> 00:09:00.039
But within about 48 hours,

00:09:00.039 --> 00:09:01.474
I started looking
at the comments,

00:09:01.474 --> 00:09:03.843 align:start size:97% position:3%
which is not something I
recommend any sane person do,

00:09:03.843 --> 00:09:05.945
but I was looking and
I saw a lot of people

00:09:05.945 --> 00:09:09.649
were kind of like it seemed
like Rubin paid attention.

00:09:09.649 --> 00:09:12.685
It seemed like he wanted to
continue the conversation.

00:09:12.685 --> 00:09:14.253
And I really did.

00:09:14.253 --> 00:09:16.322
And then I started
having conversations

00:09:16.322 --> 00:09:17.990 align:start size:94% position:6%
with some of the people
that I referenced earlier,

00:09:17.990 --> 00:09:20.159
like Shapiro and Prager and Beck

00:09:20.159 --> 00:09:21.627
and all of these people.

00:09:21.627 --> 00:09:23.396
And I realized that there
was a much wider world

00:09:23.396 --> 00:09:26.899
and a world, which
I think sorta now

00:09:26.899 --> 00:09:29.368
I can bring this into
why we're all here,

00:09:29.368 --> 00:09:31.938
a world which we
have got to save.

00:09:31.938 --> 00:09:36.475
I mean, we are handing it to
people who don't deserve it.

00:09:36.475 --> 00:09:37.944
And we all know it, right?

00:09:37.944 --> 00:09:40.246 align:start size:84% position:16%
We all know something
is very wrong

00:09:40.246 --> 00:09:44.216
and no matter what
you think you have,

00:09:44.216 --> 00:09:46.419
they want it and they
are coming for it.

00:09:46.419 --> 00:09:47.620
There is no norm.

00:09:47.620 --> 00:09:50.356 align:start size:84% position:16%
Look how different
the world is right now

00:09:50.356 --> 00:09:53.326
as we stand here on
November 1st, 2021

00:09:53.326 --> 00:09:56.662 align:start size:88% position:13%
than it was in February
of 2020, right?

00:09:56.662 --> 00:10:01.100
I mean, basically we are in
a completely different world

00:10:01.100 --> 00:10:02.335
in less than two years.

00:10:02.335 --> 00:10:03.936
Remember, we used to
talk about things,

00:10:03.936 --> 00:10:05.705 align:start size:88% position:13%
just two years ago,
less than two years ago,

00:10:05.705 --> 00:10:06.639
we had never heard the phrase

00:10:06.639 --> 00:10:07.707
two weeks to flatten the curve.

00:10:07.707 --> 00:10:09.375
Now we don't hear it anymore

00:10:09.375 --> 00:10:11.577
because they decided it was
useless, it wasn't needed.

00:10:11.577 --> 00:10:13.279 align:start size:84% position:16%
We don't talk about
herd immunity.

00:10:13.279 --> 00:10:15.381
They have just pushed
and pushed and pushed.

00:10:15.381 --> 00:10:20.386 align:start position:0%
We have guys like Fauci up
there telling us to double-mask

00:10:20.386 --> 00:10:22.355 align:start size:84% position:16%
while he's sending
emails to his friends,

00:10:22.355 --> 00:10:24.090 align:start size:84% position:16%
telling them that
the masks don't work

00:10:24.090 --> 00:10:25.324
and they actually could be worse

00:10:25.324 --> 00:10:26.926
because you might
touch your face

00:10:26.926 --> 00:10:28.394
or you'll adjust your mask more,

00:10:28.394 --> 00:10:30.963 align:start size:97% position:3%
so you do touch your face more
and that's not gonna work.

00:10:30.963 --> 00:10:33.366
And the litany, I don't have
to go into all of the things

00:10:33.366 --> 00:10:35.968 align:start size:88% position:13%
that they have all said
that they don't do.

00:10:35.968 --> 00:10:39.472 align:start size:84% position:16%
And Gavin Newsom
locking kids at home

00:10:39.472 --> 00:10:42.008
while he's eating at French
Laundry and every other,

00:10:42.008 --> 00:10:46.312 align:start size:97% position:3%
I mean, every single
Democrat politician on this.

00:10:46.312 --> 00:10:49.048
The height of absurdity as
they flaunt their own rules

00:10:49.048 --> 00:10:50.583 align:start size:84% position:16%
in our faces and
all of these things.

00:10:50.583 --> 00:10:53.419 line:0%
But look, the world is
very, very different.

00:10:53.419 --> 00:10:55.254 align:start size:94% position:6% line:0%
And the purpose, I
think, of this conference

00:10:55.254 --> 00:10:56.722 line:0%
and why I wanted to come here,

00:10:56.722 --> 00:11:00.926 align:start position:0% line:0%
even though it's perhaps a
little bit out of my main lane,

00:11:00.926 --> 00:11:05.431
is that I don't really care
what our differences are,

00:11:05.431 --> 00:11:06.666
I really don't.

00:11:06.666 --> 00:11:10.002 align:start size:84% position:16%
I know that some of
us in this room, yeah.

00:11:10.002 --> 00:11:12.738
(crowd clapping)

00:11:14.807 --> 00:11:18.244 align:start size:88% position:13%
And I don't mean that
to be glib or something,

00:11:18.244 --> 00:11:20.046
I mean that quite literally.

00:11:20.046 --> 00:11:23.315 align:start size:97% position:3%
I know we have some political
differences in this room.

00:11:23.315 --> 00:11:25.084 align:start size:94% position:6%
For those of you that
saw the panel last night,

00:11:25.084 --> 00:11:26.686
we went through some
of those differences

00:11:26.686 --> 00:11:28.354 align:start size:84% position:16%
and they are pretty
intense, right?

00:11:28.354 --> 00:11:30.790 align:start size:97% position:3%
These are deeply held
religious and philosophical

00:11:30.790 --> 00:11:32.958
and political positions
that we hold differently

00:11:32.958 --> 00:11:33.826
than each other.

00:11:33.826 --> 00:11:35.294
And that's important.

00:11:35.294 --> 00:11:37.296 align:start size:97% position:3%
So I don't wanna be dismissive
of those important issues,

00:11:37.296 --> 00:11:39.999
and we will have to deal
with all of those issues.

00:11:39.999 --> 00:11:42.535
But I think that the purpose
of this conference is to go,

00:11:42.535 --> 00:11:45.438
okay, we've got a bigger
problem at the moment.

00:11:45.438 --> 00:11:48.908
The problem is that
the same old thing

00:11:48.908 --> 00:11:52.244 align:start position:0%
that caused all of our ancestors
to come to this country,

00:11:52.244 --> 00:11:53.546 align:start size:84% position:16%
pretty much everyone
in this room,

00:11:53.546 --> 00:11:54.680
think about your ancestors.

00:11:54.680 --> 00:11:56.082
Why did they come here?

00:11:56.082 --> 00:11:57.416 align:start size:81% position:19%
Whether you're one
generation off,

00:11:57.416 --> 00:11:58.718
whether you're first generation,

00:11:58.718 --> 00:12:00.519 align:start size:81% position:19%
whether you're six
generations in,

00:12:00.519 --> 00:12:04.290 align:start size:84% position:16%
everybody in
America, in essence,

00:12:04.290 --> 00:12:06.125
with the exception
of Native Americans

00:12:06.125 --> 00:12:08.627
and African Americans,

00:12:08.627 --> 00:12:12.164 align:start size:84% position:16%
came here for a
better life by choice,

00:12:12.164 --> 00:12:14.500 align:start size:88% position:13%
they came here often
with absolutely nothing.

00:12:14.500 --> 00:12:16.035
We all know the story, right?

00:12:16.035 --> 00:12:17.503
They came with the suitcase,

00:12:17.503 --> 00:12:19.205
the clothes they had on the
back, all of that stuff.

00:12:19.205 --> 00:12:24.210 align:start position:0%
We have done an experiment that
is so profoundly impactful.

00:12:25.644 --> 00:12:28.247 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's so incredible that
we almost can't understand

00:12:28.247 --> 00:12:29.448
that it happened.

00:12:29.448 --> 00:12:31.183
We can't understand
how much better,

00:12:31.183 --> 00:12:32.384
I really believe this,

00:12:32.384 --> 00:12:34.120 align:start size:88% position:13%
how much better our
ancestors were than us,

00:12:34.120 --> 00:12:36.856 align:start size:94% position:6%
because I don't think
that most of our ancestors

00:12:36.856 --> 00:12:39.725
would be sitting around
letting this happen.

00:12:39.725 --> 00:12:41.794
My two grandfathers who
fought in World War II,

00:12:41.794 --> 00:12:43.562 align:start size:97% position:3%
I'm pretty sure they
wouldn't be sitting around.

00:12:43.562 --> 00:12:45.264 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don't know exactly
what they would be doing,

00:12:45.264 --> 00:12:47.333
but I don't think they
would be sitting around

00:12:47.333 --> 00:12:48.868
letting this happen.

00:12:48.868 --> 00:12:50.636
And we're all letting it
move on us and move on us.

00:12:50.636 --> 00:12:54.006
And that's why when
I say whatever our
differences might be,

00:12:54.006 --> 00:12:55.141
and again, not to diminish them,

00:12:55.141 --> 00:12:57.276
they are deep, they are deep.

00:12:57.276 --> 00:13:00.212
But if you would like
to save this thing,

00:13:00.212 --> 00:13:02.848 align:start size:88% position:13%
if you think that
America is worth saving,

00:13:02.848 --> 00:13:05.885
we have half the country
seemingly at the moment

00:13:05.885 --> 00:13:09.088
that does not think that
this experiment was good.

00:13:09.088 --> 00:13:11.690
And the irony, of course,
is they never leave, right?

00:13:11.690 --> 00:13:13.125
They always tell you
they're gonna leave.

00:13:13.125 --> 00:13:14.593
They always tell us...

00:13:14.593 --> 00:13:16.695
It's like, leave. I'll
buy Lena Dunham a ticket.

00:13:16.695 --> 00:13:18.931
Go, go already.

00:13:18.931 --> 00:13:22.001 align:start size:97% position:3%
Let's get someone like
Chelsea Handler, you gotta go.

00:13:22.001 --> 00:13:22.968
But they don't leave.

00:13:22.968 --> 00:13:24.170
And of course they don't leave

00:13:24.170 --> 00:13:25.938 align:start size:84% position:16%
because they have
extraordinary success,

00:13:25.938 --> 00:13:28.440
extraordinary wealth,
extraordinary health,

00:13:28.440 --> 00:13:29.675
all of these things,

00:13:29.675 --> 00:13:32.111
the things that they
only take for granted

00:13:32.111 --> 00:13:35.447
because of our success.

00:13:35.447 --> 00:13:38.250 align:start size:94% position:6%
So whatever our political
differences are,

00:13:38.250 --> 00:13:39.952
we've got to put them
aside at the moment.

00:13:39.952 --> 00:13:42.521
And then I would say, if we
can get some of these wins,

00:13:42.521 --> 00:13:45.591 align:start size:94% position:6%
so let's say Youngkin
actually wins in Virginia

00:13:45.591 --> 00:13:47.693
and it sends a signal, right?

00:13:47.693 --> 00:13:50.296
It sends a signal
across the country.

00:13:50.296 --> 00:13:52.164
Holy cow, holy cow,

00:13:52.164 --> 00:13:56.068 align:start size:94% position:6%
maybe there's a real
pushback against wokeness.

00:13:56.068 --> 00:13:58.871
The system that we have,
the Federalist system,

00:13:58.871 --> 00:14:01.473 align:start size:97% position:3%
that these states are supposed
to operate independently,

00:14:01.473 --> 00:14:02.708
in some ways it's working

00:14:02.708 --> 00:14:04.210 align:start size:84% position:16%
at its highest level
right now, right?

00:14:04.210 --> 00:14:06.245 align:start size:97% position:3%
The states are so profoundly
different right now

00:14:06.245 --> 00:14:07.479
that in many ways,

00:14:07.479 --> 00:14:08.447
it's like being in
different countries.

00:14:08.447 --> 00:14:10.616
When I'm in California,

00:14:10.616 --> 00:14:13.986 align:start size:97% position:3%
it feels dark and depressing
and everyone's masked.

00:14:13.986 --> 00:14:15.221
And you can sorta...

00:14:15.221 --> 00:14:17.690 align:start size:84% position:16%
I actually don't leave
my house that often

00:14:17.690 --> 00:14:19.525 align:start size:84% position:16%
because there's
just not much to do

00:14:19.525 --> 00:14:21.527
and I don't feel like being
around a lot of these people.

00:14:21.527 --> 00:14:23.062
But when I do go shopping,

00:14:23.062 --> 00:14:24.530
you see people and
they've got the mask

00:14:24.530 --> 00:14:26.332
and they kind of
look glossed over.

00:14:26.332 --> 00:14:27.733 align:start size:84% position:16%
They don't look like
they're thinking,

00:14:27.733 --> 00:14:29.368
they look deeply depressed.

00:14:29.368 --> 00:14:30.536
You see this almost everywhere.

00:14:30.536 --> 00:14:31.770
I live in Los Angeles,

00:14:31.770 --> 00:14:35.407
which is a particular
brand of the craziness.

00:14:35.407 --> 00:14:37.676 align:start size:97% position:3%
But in some ways, it shows
you that the system's working,

00:14:37.676 --> 00:14:40.512 align:start size:84% position:16%
these people seemingly
want it, right?

00:14:40.512 --> 00:14:44.083 align:start size:84% position:16%
Larry Elder ran a
great campaign, I
think, for the recall.

00:14:44.083 --> 00:14:46.218
It did not go well, obviously.

00:14:46.218 --> 00:14:47.686
I campaigned with Larry,

00:14:47.686 --> 00:14:50.222 align:start size:84% position:16%
and the way the
media treated Larry,

00:14:50.222 --> 00:14:51.724
the L.A. Times calling him

00:14:51.724 --> 00:14:53.559
the blackface of
white supremacy.

00:14:53.559 --> 00:14:56.862 align:start size:97% position:3%
I mean, yeah, like stuff that
you truly cannot imagine.

00:14:56.862 --> 00:14:59.632
Joe Biden showing up a
day before the recall,

00:14:59.632 --> 00:15:02.134
refusing to even say
Larry Elder's name

00:15:02.134 --> 00:15:04.136
and calling him a Trump clone,

00:15:04.136 --> 00:15:06.338
a man who grew up in
South Central L.A.,

00:15:06.338 --> 00:15:08.941
the son of a janitor
came from nothing,

00:15:08.941 --> 00:15:10.676 align:start size:84% position:16%
who has made himself
into, I think,

00:15:10.676 --> 00:15:14.513
one of the best public thinkers
that we have in the country,

00:15:14.513 --> 00:15:15.714
the way they dismissed him

00:15:15.714 --> 00:15:17.683 align:start size:84% position:16%
and attacked him
and everything else.

00:15:17.683 --> 00:15:18.951
But I mention all that

00:15:18.951 --> 00:15:20.452
because California
seems to want it.

00:15:20.452 --> 00:15:22.988 align:start size:84% position:16%
They've sort of
made their decision.

00:15:22.988 --> 00:15:25.491 align:start size:94% position:6%
We like this. We like
this ever expanding state.

00:15:25.491 --> 00:15:26.792
We like the school boards

00:15:26.792 --> 00:15:28.961
that have complete
control over us.

00:15:28.961 --> 00:15:31.130 align:start size:84% position:16%
We'd rather talk
about gender pronouns

00:15:31.130 --> 00:15:32.364
than fixing the streets

00:15:32.364 --> 00:15:33.666
or getting the homeless
people off the streets

00:15:33.666 --> 00:15:36.168 align:start size:84% position:16%
or the drugs or the
crime that's going up.

00:15:36.168 --> 00:15:40.239
We bring in the DA who
ruined San Francisco.

00:15:40.239 --> 00:15:41.674 align:start size:81% position:19%
I mean, literally,
San Francisco,

00:15:41.674 --> 00:15:43.409 align:start size:97% position:3%
which I was also in San
Francisco a couple weeks ago,

00:15:43.409 --> 00:15:45.311
which is a dystopian nightmare.

00:15:45.311 --> 00:15:46.845
It looks like "Blade Runner".

00:15:46.845 --> 00:15:49.648 align:start position:0%
It is just an absolute
nightmare. Well, what happened?

00:15:49.648 --> 00:15:54.119 align:start size:97% position:3%
The DA of San Francisco
became the DA of Los Angeles.

00:15:54.119 --> 00:15:56.121
Bernie backed DA's
name as George Gascon

00:15:56.121 --> 00:15:57.957 align:start size:84% position:16%
and now you're allowed
to, in essence,

00:15:57.957 --> 00:16:02.294
steal up to, I think, it's
850 or $900 worth of stuff

00:16:02.294 --> 00:16:03.595
and they will not prosecute you.

00:16:03.595 --> 00:16:05.731
So you can basically
walk into Best Buy

00:16:05.731 --> 00:16:07.967 align:start size:88% position:13%
and steal a PlayStation
5 and four games.

00:16:07.967 --> 00:16:09.068
But if you steal a fifth game,

00:16:09.068 --> 00:16:11.170
then they're gonna get on you.

00:16:11.170 --> 00:16:13.305 align:start size:84% position:16%
It is just absolutely
incredible.

00:16:13.305 --> 00:16:14.540
But I mention this

00:16:14.540 --> 00:16:17.609 align:start size:84% position:16%
because the experiment
is kind of working.

00:16:17.609 --> 00:16:20.446
California is getting
what it asked for.

00:16:20.446 --> 00:16:23.048 line:0%
New York is getting
what it asked for.

00:16:23.048 --> 00:16:24.516 align:start size:84% position:16% line:0%
It's funny, as I'm
sure many of you know,

00:16:24.516 --> 00:16:25.451 line:0%
I was off the grid.

00:16:25.451 --> 00:16:26.685 line:0%
I do this August off the grid,

00:16:26.685 --> 00:16:28.787 line:0%
no phone, no news,
nothing, every year.

00:16:28.787 --> 00:16:30.723
I've done it for five years.

00:16:30.723 --> 00:16:32.558
When I came back this
year on September 1st,

00:16:32.558 --> 00:16:34.793
Adam Carolla hosted my show

00:16:34.793 --> 00:16:36.462 align:start size:94% position:6%
and he told me
everything that I missed.

00:16:36.462 --> 00:16:38.597 align:start size:84% position:16%
And he told me
about Andrew Cuomo,

00:16:38.597 --> 00:16:40.099
in essence, being taken out.

00:16:40.099 --> 00:16:41.767
And I didn't know who the
Lieutenant Governor was.

00:16:41.767 --> 00:16:43.202
I didn't know if it
was a man or a woman.

00:16:43.202 --> 00:16:45.104 align:start size:94% position:6%
I knew absolutely
nothing about the person,

00:16:45.104 --> 00:16:47.006
but I said to him before
he even told me anything,

00:16:47.006 --> 00:16:51.543
I said, "I guarantee
you, whoever it is,
it will be worse."

00:16:51.543 --> 00:16:54.380
And congratulations, New
York, it is worse, right?

00:16:54.380 --> 00:16:55.948
I mean, they're, yeah.

00:16:55.948 --> 00:16:57.783
(crowd clapping)

00:16:57.783 --> 00:16:58.984
So that's the point.

00:16:58.984 --> 00:17:01.053 align:start size:88% position:13%
The states in many ways
are breaking apart.

00:17:01.053 --> 00:17:02.688
Now I wanna keep
this union, right?

00:17:02.688 --> 00:17:04.656 align:start size:88% position:13%
We're called the United
States of America.

00:17:04.656 --> 00:17:06.859
United is first. We should
keep this thing together.

00:17:06.859 --> 00:17:08.427
We need some of that glue.

00:17:08.427 --> 00:17:09.928
We've got to do this,

00:17:09.928 --> 00:17:12.398 align:start size:97% position:3%
or we'll be in some sort of
perpetual low-grade civil war.

00:17:12.398 --> 00:17:13.799
That will not be good.

00:17:13.799 --> 00:17:15.300
The challenge on us, I think,

00:17:15.300 --> 00:17:17.469
is as the states kind of go
in these different directions

00:17:17.469 --> 00:17:20.172
and as a sort of new,
I would say broader,

00:17:20.172 --> 00:17:22.741
hopefully conservative
movement comes together,

00:17:22.741 --> 00:17:24.576 align:start size:84% position:16%
the real question
will be, well, okay,

00:17:24.576 --> 00:17:27.179
if certain places,
let's say, Florida

00:17:27.179 --> 00:17:30.115 align:start size:97% position:3%
is I would say the
pinnacle of doing it right,

00:17:30.115 --> 00:17:32.684 align:start size:97% position:3%
and Ron DeSantis, I
actually met him last week,

00:17:32.684 --> 00:17:35.054
this is a good, decent man

00:17:35.054 --> 00:17:37.189
and I hope he will
run for president.

00:17:37.189 --> 00:17:39.958
(crowd clapping)

00:17:43.695 --> 00:17:45.497 align:start size:81% position:19%
I hope he will
run for president.

00:17:45.497 --> 00:17:48.233 align:start size:97% position:3%
And I also think that
whether he does or doesn't,

00:17:48.233 --> 00:17:49.735 align:start size:84% position:16%
wherever Trump
fits into all that,

00:17:49.735 --> 00:17:52.805 align:start size:97% position:3%
the crop of Republicans coming
up is really, really strong

00:17:52.805 --> 00:17:55.007
and good and diverse
in the right sense,

00:17:55.007 --> 00:17:58.277
not in the sense of the
word that the left uses.

00:17:58.277 --> 00:18:00.345
But as the states go
off in different ways,

00:18:00.345 --> 00:18:01.580
the challenge will be, okay,

00:18:01.580 --> 00:18:02.915
so if Florida is
gonna do it right,

00:18:02.915 --> 00:18:04.249
and Tennessee is
gonna do it right

00:18:04.249 --> 00:18:05.918
and Texas is gonna do it right,

00:18:05.918 --> 00:18:08.821
well, will the other
guys leave us alone?

00:18:08.821 --> 00:18:10.489
And I don't think
the answer is yes.

00:18:10.489 --> 00:18:12.658
As a matter of fact, I'm
sure the answer is no.

00:18:12.658 --> 00:18:15.694
The more successful that
Florida continues to be,

00:18:15.694 --> 00:18:19.631 align:start position:0%
as it brings in police officers
and EMT people and nurses

00:18:19.631 --> 00:18:22.067
that are getting fired for
making personal decisions,

00:18:22.067 --> 00:18:24.169
as Florida brings
them in, yeah...

00:18:24.169 --> 00:18:25.471
(crowd clapping)

00:18:25.471 --> 00:18:27.873
As Florida brings them
in and become stronger

00:18:27.873 --> 00:18:30.476
and becomes a state where
the rule of law matters

00:18:30.476 --> 00:18:32.177
and basic truth matters

00:18:32.177 --> 00:18:34.980 align:start size:94% position:6%
and we're not gonna
teach children neo racism

00:18:34.980 --> 00:18:35.914
and the rest of it.

00:18:35.914 --> 00:18:38.450
As these states do these things

00:18:38.450 --> 00:18:40.252
and I do think hopefully
it will start happening

00:18:40.252 --> 00:18:42.821
in Virginia now too
if today goes well,

00:18:42.821 --> 00:18:44.723 align:start size:94% position:6%
the other states, they're
not gonna be happy

00:18:44.723 --> 00:18:45.791
with that success.

00:18:45.791 --> 00:18:47.326
They will not leave that alone.

00:18:47.326 --> 00:18:48.594
So I think our next challenge

00:18:48.594 --> 00:18:50.496
that we should start
thinking about now

00:18:50.496 --> 00:18:52.965 align:start size:84% position:16%
is if you live in
one of these states,

00:18:52.965 --> 00:18:54.766
figure out how to
defend that state.

00:18:54.766 --> 00:18:56.235
I mean that sort
